# Damped spring, adaptive Dormand–Prince RK45 from 0 to 100 s.
# Matched settings: Fermium's error control is purely relative (D17), so the Julia, Python and SciPy
# versions use the same kind of control, rtol = 1e-6 with atol = 1e-30.
# Exact solution: x(100 s) = 1.1176166148e-12 m. Measured: Fermium 1.11735e-12 m (relative error 2.4e-4,
# 4297 steps); Julia/Python/SciPy 1.11745e-12 m (relative error 1.5e-4, 4903 steps). Comparable accuracy,
# not identical: the step-size controllers differ.
m = 1 kg
k = 100 N/m
b = 0.5 kg/s
t0 = clock()
solve m x'' = -k x - b x'
  with x(0) = 0.1 m, x'(0) = 0 m/s
  for t from 0 s to 100 s tolerance 1e-6
t1 = clock()
print "x_100s", x(100 s) / (1 m) to 10 digits
print "accepted_steps", len(x) - 1
print "TIME_INNER", (t1 - t0) / (1 s)
